# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A .gitignore for writers
# Annotated version of Chapter 10.3
#
# Git ignores every line starting with #, so you can leave the
# comments in. Delete the patterns you don't need.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Operating system clutter.
# These appear without your asking and change constantly.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor files.
# Swap files, workspace settings, and tool-specific folders.
.vscode/
.obsidian/
*.swp
*~

# Exports.
# These are outputs, regenerable from the source (Ch. 25).
# Chapter 10.2 explains why committing them is a mistake.
*.docx
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
exports/
manuscript.md

# Word lock files.
# The hidden file Word creates while a document is open.
~$*.docx

# Keep the reference document.
# The exception to *.docx above — it's a style template, not an export.
# Chapter 25.6 explains what it is.
!reference.docx

# Scratch and backups.
scratch/
*.bak

# Research material (non-fiction).
# Working material rather than deliverables — see Chapter 27.1.
# Uncomment if you keep scans and photographs in the project folder.
# research/

# Large assets — uncomment if you are NOT using Git LFS.
# Chapter 27.2 covers LFS; Chapter 10.2 explains why size matters.
# *.psd
# *.tif
# *.tiff
